e change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e37c1aea9388cdbe89841a8e10d9954c6526a32ace1084811f786b588da9146"} {"question" "q-113557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ to $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=3{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot (-5)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=3{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e37c1aea9388cdbe89841a8e10d9954c6526a32ace1084811f786b588da9146"} {"question" "q-82599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ to $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-8)-(-3)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e37c1aea9388cdbe89841a8e10d9954c6526a32ace1084811f786b588da9146"} {"question" "q-113573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 42\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-113573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ to $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is given below. Find $[x]_{B}$ given that $x=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 6-5\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $x=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e37c1aea9388cdbe89841a8e10d9954c6526a32ace1084811f786b588da9146"} {"question" "q-82705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066197/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b0efdf32801874ff6ad6af337dfd37977788fadde3dd9557fc2c8bd8766293e"} {"question" "q-82705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/hom